27
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:46,370
[Previously on Knot]

28
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,400
This necklace was worn by Saengnuea.

29
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:48,430
If it's really the same necklace,

30
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:50,000
then it means Saengnuea

31
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:52,000
must have been at the bar that night.

32
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,460
Send him the location.

33
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:59,000
Where should I put Jim's little prince?

34
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:00,060
How about here?

35
00:02:02,550 --> 00:02:05,670
Where are you going, Mr. Phatsa?

36
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:10,190
Nakhun and the others forgot their documents.

37
00:02:10,210 --> 00:02:12,530
I'm driving over to deliver them now.

38
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:13,800
Okay.

39
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:32,960
Jim.

40
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:33,630
Hey.

41
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:34,460
Are you okay?

42
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:35,990
I'm fine.

43
00:02:36,010 --> 00:02:37,350
They're all broken.

44
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,900
Jim's little princes.

45
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:41,850
God bless.

46
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:42,720
God bless.

47
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:45,260
God bless.

48
00:02:45,610 --> 00:02:46,750
Oh my god.

49
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:48,829
Jim.

50
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:49,630
What's wrong?

51
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:51,730
Please help me clean this up.

52
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,200
Okay, Mr. Phatsa.

53
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,600
Drive safely.

54
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:58,520
What should I do?

55
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,360
Who are you?

56
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:30,990
You'll know soon enough.

57
00:03:30,990 --> 00:03:31,790
Get down!

58
00:03:31,810 --> 00:03:32,200
Run!

59
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,130
Catch him!

60
00:03:45,130 --> 00:03:46,380
Hurry, hurry!

61
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:04,830
Catch him!

62
00:04:05,630 --> 00:04:06,330
Hurry!

63
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,170
Tim, how dare you betray our family!

64
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:30,500
Shut up, you little brat.

65
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:32,700
Who betrayed who?

66
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,860
The one who sold out the family's information

67
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:37,330
has no right to scold me.

68
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,860
What nonsense are you talking about?

69
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,730
When did I ever sell information?

70
00:04:47,730 --> 00:04:49,750
You were just seduced a little,

71
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,230
you stupid Alpha,

72
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:55,460
and you spilled the whole itinerary.

73
00:04:56,090 --> 00:04:57,200
What a coincidence.

74
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,000
Yeah.

75
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,380
Or should I say,

76
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,560
I shouldn't think this is a coincidence?

77
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,490
I'm going out of town next week.

78
00:05:03,510 --> 00:05:05,080
Is your whole family going?

79
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:25,230
Which day are you leaving?

80
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:28,440
Which day?

81
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:29,420
Saturday?

82
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:30,840
Saturday.

83
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,490
Bastard!

84
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:49,659
Naphitch!

85
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:54,110
What do you mean by that?

86
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:59,450
It means your favorite brother

87
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:04,400
sold the secret just to sleep with an Omega.

88
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:06,660
Scum!

89
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:09,810
You have a death wish!

90
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:21,830
Naphitch!

91
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,730
Calm down.

92
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,890
Naphitch, bring it here.

93
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,850
Naphitch!

94
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:41,470
Is that all you've got?

95
00:06:42,159 --> 00:06:43,770
You lose control

96
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:45,860
when you smell a familiar scent.

97
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:51,960
Naphitch!

98
00:06:57,810 --> 00:06:59,350
Brother, I can't do it.

99
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:07,290
Snap out of it. Look at me.

100
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:12,650
Naphitch, stay awake.

101
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:19,930
Control it.

102
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:23,030
Don't let your instincts control you.

103
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:28,320
Wait a minute.

104
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:30,050
Why do you have

105
00:07:30,070 --> 00:07:31,270
Saengnuea's things?

106
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,530
So what?

107
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,890
Are you and Saengnuea...

108
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,700
Hahahaha.

109
00:07:37,930 --> 00:07:39,260
You finally guessed it.

110
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:40,500
You and Saengnuea

111
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:43,260
have been working together all along.

112
00:07:45,909 --> 00:07:47,610
We are brothers.

113
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:51,730
There's no need to use the word "working together".

114
00:08:00,050 --> 00:08:01,400
What exactly do you want?

115
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,860
Why are you doing all this?

116
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,860
If my life is ruined,

117
00:08:05,910 --> 00:08:07,840
the people who destroyed my family

118
00:08:08,130 --> 00:08:09,350
must go down with me.

119
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:10,520
Are you crazy?

120
00:08:11,050 --> 00:08:12,780
Our family gave you a chance.

121
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,900
From having nothing,

122
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,260
we made you the manager of the bar.

123
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,380
The land where you built the bar

124
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,410
originally belonged to my dad.

125
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:22,840
Before you took it over,

126
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:25,200
that land was ours.

127
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:28,190
Your dad mortgaged it himself

128
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:31,560
because he lost everything gambling.

129
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:33,299
Our family bought it back,

130
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,659
which is why we let you manage it.

131
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,000
The title deed has always been

132
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,059
under the Devathitirat family's name.

133
00:08:39,059 --> 00:08:41,190
You only make excuses for yourselves.

134
00:08:41,799 --> 00:08:43,400
I am the one who was deceived.

135
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,560
I was scammed out of everything.

136
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,800
If you want to blame someone,

137
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,800
blame your dad.

138
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,330
He caused his wife and children

139
00:08:52,930 --> 00:08:54,100
to end up like this.

140
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:58,160
It's all because of you

141
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,020
that my boss ended up like this today.

142
00:09:01,530 --> 00:09:03,260
If anything happens to my boss,

143
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:04,990
you'll have to go down with him.

144
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:06,260
Boss?

145
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:08,860
So this isn't just a personal grudge.

146
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:54,160
Nakhin, take Naphitch away.

147
00:09:59,930 --> 00:10:00,730
No, brother.

148
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,730
I want to stay and help brother Nakhun.

149
00:10:03,730 --> 00:10:05,730
If we stay any longer, we'll all die.

150
00:10:06,490 --> 00:10:07,290
Go!

151
00:10:07,810 --> 00:10:08,800
No, brother.

152
00:10:08,950 --> 00:10:10,080
Let me go.

153
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,200
Nakhun!

154
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:14,800
Brother, let me go.

155
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,250
Come on, Naphitch.

156
00:10:16,330 --> 00:10:18,590
Naphitch, run!

157
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,160
Ongsa, what's wrong?

158
00:10:33,330 --> 00:10:34,700
Phatsa,

159
00:10:34,730 --> 00:10:37,080
I feel like something's wrong with Saengnuea.

160
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:37,920
A few days ago, Nakhin said

161
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:38,790
he smelled Saengnuea's scent

162
00:10:38,790 --> 00:10:40,260
on Naphitch.

163
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:42,840
But they shouldn't even know each other.

164
00:10:43,230 --> 00:10:44,030
Could it be

165
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,200
that Saengnuea is secretly

166
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,200
flirting with Naphitch behind everyone's back?

167
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:49,370
So I looked into it,

168
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:52,160
and I found out something even bigger.

169
00:10:52,230 --> 00:10:53,230
What did you find?

170
00:10:53,470 --> 00:10:54,830
Saengnuea

171
00:10:54,850 --> 00:10:57,190
grew up with Tim's family.

172
00:10:57,430 --> 00:10:58,840
What do you mean?

173
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:00,280
Saengnuea's father

174
00:11:00,310 --> 00:11:03,320
entrusted his land to Tim's family,

175
00:11:03,350 --> 00:11:04,610
on the condition that Tim

176
00:11:04,610 --> 00:11:06,220
must take care of Saengnuea.

177
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:08,890
Could it be

178
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:10,570
that Saengnuea

179
00:11:10,590 --> 00:11:13,090
is the real mastermind behind all this?

180
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:16,090
Even the prostitution frame-up might have been planned by him.

181
00:11:16,090 --> 00:11:22,330
Damn it. Then Nakhun...

182
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:38,360
Ongsa.

183
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,260
What happened?

184
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:45,420
You look like the old prime minister got re-elected.

185
00:11:45,930 --> 00:11:46,730
You brat.

186
00:11:47,730 --> 00:11:50,060
I'm trying to piece everything together.

187
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,460
Naphitch's incident,

188
00:11:53,050 --> 00:11:54,000
Mai,

189
00:11:54,930 --> 00:11:55,800
and Tim.

190
00:11:57,930 --> 00:12:00,500
It feels like everything is connected.

191
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:03,560
It really is.

192
00:12:04,730 --> 00:12:05,680
That day, Saengnuea

193
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,940
was acting weird when he came to the shop.

194
00:12:10,190 --> 00:12:10,990
How so?

195
00:12:11,050 --> 00:12:13,790
The day you and Nakhin kissed.

196
00:12:16,730 --> 00:12:18,230
When Saengnuea came,

197
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,360
he asked me to pack a cake for him to take away.

198
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:25,180
I turned around to pack the cake for just a moment,

199
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:28,060
and when I looked back, he was gone.

200
00:12:28,930 --> 00:12:30,530
He probably went home first.

201
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,620
Yeah.

202
00:12:32,770 --> 00:12:34,620
And it seemed like he left

203
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,570
before Nakhin's brother arrived.

204
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,400
No.

205
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,320
As soon as he saw Naphitch,

206
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,320
he left in a hurry.

207
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,520
Yeah.

208
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:50,260
I didn't even get the money for the cake.

209
00:12:52,510 --> 00:12:58,070
In that case, it's not a coincidence.

210
00:13:02,130 --> 00:13:05,460
Ongsa, should we still ask for the cake money?

211
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:06,890
No need.

212
00:13:09,010 --> 00:13:11,070
Nile, pack up and go home early today.

213
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:13,920
But it's not closing time yet.

214
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:17,820
I'm going to close the shop and go back too. Don't worry.

215
00:13:17,970 --> 00:13:23,160
Be careful on your way home. Remember to lock the door.

216
00:13:23,190 --> 00:13:25,670
If anything happens,

217
00:13:27,530 --> 00:13:28,330
call me.

218
00:13:29,090 --> 00:13:29,890
Okay.

219
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,360
Bye.

220
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:36,720
What should we do now?

221
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,320
Jim.

222
00:13:44,350 --> 00:13:45,150
What's wrong?

223
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:50,000
Why is it so quiet at home? Where is everyone?

224
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:53,840
Nakhun, Nakhin,

225
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:54,840
and Naphitch

226
00:13:54,870 --> 00:13:57,050
went out early to look at the land.

227
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:02,470
What about the bodyguards? Sila and Ai?

228
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,990
Mr. Naret called them to look for

229
00:14:06,010 --> 00:14:07,440
the Pure Omega.

230
00:14:07,490 --> 00:14:13,010
So there's no one home, that's why it's so quiet.

231
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,160
What about Phatsa?

232
00:14:17,030 --> 00:14:18,910
Phatsa

233
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:21,210
went to deliver documents to Mr. Nakhun.

234
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,600
It's so late, and he's not back yet.

235
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:47,790
I hope nothing bad happens.

236
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,990
May the gods keep my children safe.

237
00:15:28,590 --> 00:15:29,390
How is it?

238
00:15:29,950 --> 00:15:31,160
We're close to finding that

239
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,710
Pure Omega.

240
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,820
Our men found clues about the vehicle transporting him

241
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:38,110
and started picking up the Omega's scent.

242
00:15:38,110 --> 00:15:40,880
We should be able to bring him back soon.

243
00:15:41,550 --> 00:15:42,350
Good.

244
00:15:43,330 --> 00:15:44,730
Then don't delay.

245
00:15:45,730 --> 00:15:47,660
Bring him back as soon as possible.

246
00:15:48,330 --> 00:15:50,190
I don't care what methods you use.

247
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:51,750
Yes, sir.

248
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:53,950
Before it's too late,

249
00:15:53,950 --> 00:15:56,460
this Pure Omega

250
00:15:56,490 --> 00:15:58,600
must marry Nakhin.

251
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:02,460
We can't let him belong to anyone else.

252
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:06,250
Understood. We'll get on it right away.

253
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:23,130
Phatsa.

254
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:25,760
What happened?

255
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:28,160
Don't go in yet.

256
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:31,380
Get out of here quickly.

257
00:16:31,930 --> 00:16:35,020
Nakhun used himself as bait

258
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:36,600
to hold off Tim and his men,

259
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,760
so Nakhin and I could escape.

260
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:41,260
Damn it.

261
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,560
Trying to be a hero, Nakhun?

262
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:53,660
Your epitaph

263
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,430
will surely be cool.

264
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:02,490
At least it won't say I'm a stray dog like you.

265
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:05,260
Ah!

266
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,900
This series of events

267
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:20,290
is probably related to Saengnuea.

268
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:34,390
Nakhun!

269
00:17:34,410 --> 00:17:34,940
Get down!

270
00:17:40,010 --> 00:17:40,810
Nakhun!

271
00:17:41,290 --> 00:17:42,710
Are you okay?

272
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:44,660
Phatsa.

273
00:17:46,410 --> 00:17:48,200
We need to leave here immediately.

274
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,260
Nakhin,

275
00:17:49,290 --> 00:17:50,540
you take Naphitch

276
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:52,130
to Ongsa's shop.

277
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:54,640
Phatsa and I will follow in the car. Go!

278
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,040
Go!

279
00:17:57,930 --> 00:17:59,220
Be careful.

280
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:04,860
Can you hold on?

281
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:08,860
Let's just escape first.

282
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:10,300
They're catching up.

283
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:24,430
Abandon the car.

284
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:25,800
Hurry.

285
00:18:57,730 --> 00:18:59,460
Would you like anything today?

286
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,400
I'll make you a drink.

287
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:09,330
I just came to take a look.

288
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:17,250
Ongsa, why are you so nervous?

289
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,530
It's not my first time here.

290
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:29,270
Your shop is really cozy.

291
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:33,090
It suits you well.

292
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,260
Is something on your mind?

293
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:42,060
If there's anything,

294
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:45,130
you can tell me directly.

295
00:19:52,330 --> 00:19:55,130
Of course I will.

296
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:57,420
But lately,

297
00:19:57,450 --> 00:20:02,760
I feel like you've gotten bolder, Ongsa.

298
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:08,710
Or is it because someone is backing you up?

299
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:13,760
No, not backing you up.

300
00:20:16,130 --> 00:20:18,390
I should say, a Beta

301
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:23,130
daring to stand beside a True Alpha.

302
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,530
You seem to have forgotten.

303
00:20:29,930 --> 00:20:31,060
This world

304
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:35,180
has its own hierarchy.

305
00:20:36,910 --> 00:20:39,160
Who should stand where,

306
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:42,480
and who should be with whom.

307
00:20:45,530 --> 00:20:47,980
A relationship like this

308
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:52,010
won't last long.

309
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:56,880
Logically speaking,

310
00:20:56,900 --> 00:21:02,600
a real True Alpha

311
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:10,960
should be with a suitable Omega.

312
00:21:14,730 --> 00:21:15,900
An Omega.

313
00:21:20,150 --> 00:21:21,590
Like me.

314
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:27,460
What are you hiding from?

315
00:21:32,230 --> 00:21:35,830
I don't know what's wrong with you now.

316
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:41,460
Why would you say such things?

317
00:21:42,490 --> 00:21:44,900
Nakhin sees me for who I am,

318
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:46,860
not my secondary gender.

319
00:21:47,150 --> 00:21:48,780
That's innate.

320
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,400
Who you are?

321
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,510
Someone without pheromones,

322
00:21:53,510 --> 00:21:55,970
who can't smell others' pheromones either.

323
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:01,130
Even if you love them to death,

324
00:22:03,290 --> 00:22:07,440
you will never smell your lover's pheromones.

325
00:22:09,110 --> 00:22:11,420
And the person you love

326
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:16,510
will never be captivated by your scent.

327
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:26,150
Love without physical attraction,

328
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:28,400
without instinct,

329
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:31,960
without physical response,

330
00:22:33,780 --> 00:22:36,110
how long can it last?

331
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:45,090
Even if I can't smell his scent,

332
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,660
or he won't be obsessed with mine,

333
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,930
our feelings

334
00:22:53,130 --> 00:22:54,860
are no less than anyone else's.

335
00:22:56,370 --> 00:22:57,640
Ridiculous.

336
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:00,010
Sounds like a novel.

337
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:14,090
I chose Ongsa.

338
00:23:16,330 --> 00:23:20,690
My love never needs anyone's approval,

339
00:23:20,710 --> 00:23:22,990
especially from someone like you.

340
00:23:24,730 --> 00:23:28,050
My love with Ongsa belongs to our hearts,

341
00:23:28,070 --> 00:23:31,960
not trapped in a cage of Omegas, Alphas,

342
00:23:31,980 --> 00:23:35,480
or True Alphas.

343
00:23:38,190 --> 00:23:42,810
How touching. A mighty True Alpha

344
00:23:42,830 --> 00:23:45,890
is willing to stoop down and hold a Beta's hand.

345
00:23:47,700 --> 00:23:49,600
But facts are facts.

346
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:53,020
Betas can't have children.

347
00:23:53,050 --> 00:24:00,130
In the end, your family bloodline will end.

348
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:05,330
Because you chose someone with no bloodline value.

349
00:24:08,130 --> 00:24:10,930
I wasn't born to reproduce.

350
00:24:12,130 --> 00:24:13,160
I was born to love.

351
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:16,630
And the person I love is Ongsa.

352
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,400
I love with my heart,

353
00:24:21,330 --> 00:24:23,200
not with beastly instincts.

354
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:27,850
Now, let's talk about something more important.

355
00:24:28,810 --> 00:24:29,810
Tim.

356
00:24:35,310 --> 00:24:37,890
Tim? Who is he?

357
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:41,830
Saengnuea, your memory

358
00:24:41,850 --> 00:24:43,500
doesn't seem very good.

359
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:48,330
The older brother who raised you since childhood,

360
00:24:49,730 --> 00:24:51,160
you can even forget him.

361
00:24:52,100 --> 00:24:54,730
He's just the son of my dad's old subordinate.

362
00:24:56,030 --> 00:25:01,230
When I was young, I was only occasionally sent to live at his house,

363
00:25:02,890 --> 00:25:03,690
that's all.

364
00:25:04,450 --> 00:25:05,670
Is that really it?

365
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:10,200
Because their family owed ours a favor.

366
00:25:11,420 --> 00:25:15,400
My dad helped their family, his parents,

367
00:25:15,430 --> 00:25:19,030
so Tim bore the responsibility of repaying the debt since childhood.

368
00:25:19,030 --> 00:25:20,670
That's all.

369
00:25:21,330 --> 00:25:22,990
What about that piece of land?

370
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:30,390
That land was my family's only remaining inheritance.

371
00:25:31,660 --> 00:25:34,930
But that fool mortgaged it

372
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:37,560
and watched it fall into someone else's hands.

373
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:39,610
In the end, it fell into

374
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:42,900
the dirty hands of the Devathitirat family.

375
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:46,720
Later, they even built a bar there

376
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:48,360
and let Tim manage it.

377
00:25:51,770 --> 00:25:54,620
Do you know what this is like?

378
00:25:56,270 --> 00:26:01,590
It's like you trample on my family's dignity every day.

379
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,660
If that's really the case,

380
00:26:05,130 --> 00:26:07,390
why didn't you say so from the beginning?

381
00:26:07,700 --> 00:26:09,700
Why drag other people into this?

382
00:26:10,710 --> 00:26:11,510
Speak.

383
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:14,240
What would saying it change?

384
00:26:15,060 --> 00:26:17,580
Would the words of a down-and-out Omega like me

385
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:19,010
reach the ears of

386
00:26:19,030 --> 00:26:20,910
you upper-class Alphas?

387
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:23,130
How could the truth help me?

388
00:26:23,940 --> 00:26:26,810
You have the right to choose,

389
00:26:27,430 --> 00:26:29,290
the right to possess everything,

390
00:26:29,470 --> 00:26:30,870
the right to love anyone,

391
00:26:32,570 --> 00:26:34,630
and the right to do whatever you want.

392
00:26:36,050 --> 00:26:37,850
You can trample on others at will

393
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,660
and call it all business.

394
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:42,190
But someone like me

395
00:26:42,210 --> 00:26:44,930
can't even protect what's mine.

396
00:26:45,610 --> 00:26:50,040
I don't even have the right to grieve with dignity.

397
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:53,820
Even if you've been hurt,

398
00:26:53,850 --> 00:26:56,880
it's no excuse to hurt others.

399
00:26:57,030 --> 00:27:00,630
Is that so? Then pray

400
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:02,300
that your rule-breaking

401
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:06,040
love for a Beta is strong enough

402
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:10,760
to survive what's coming.

403
00:27:18,730 --> 00:27:20,130
Let me ask you seriously.

404
00:27:21,060 --> 00:27:22,680
What exactly is your relationship

405
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:24,080
with Tim?

406
00:27:25,860 --> 00:27:27,390
Why ask this all of a sudden?

407
00:27:27,910 --> 00:27:28,710
Nonsense.

408
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,530
This isn't nonsense at all.

409
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:36,680
Many things are connected,

410
00:27:36,700 --> 00:27:41,760
including Tim, the bar, Mai,

411
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:44,200
and you.

412
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:48,490
You know a few fragments

413
00:27:48,520 --> 00:27:50,450
and think you know everything?

414
00:27:52,230 --> 00:27:56,920
At least I know you're hiding a secret.

415
00:27:59,080 --> 00:28:01,060
And this secret has to do with Tim.

416
00:28:01,830 --> 00:28:03,600
There are some things

417
00:28:03,630 --> 00:28:06,660
a Beta like you can't understand.

418
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:11,900
Don't meddle in a world that isn't yours.

419
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:54,780
Are you scared?

420
00:28:55,660 --> 00:28:56,960
Of course I am.

421
00:28:58,100 --> 00:28:59,760
We can't just keep running.

422
00:29:00,730 --> 00:29:01,930
We have to fight them.

423
00:29:03,130 --> 00:29:04,390
But most importantly,

424
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:08,200
we must go back together.

425
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:23,400
Stay close to me.

426
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:25,900
Always.

427
00:30:14,130 --> 00:30:15,230
Nice shooting.

428
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:19,000
You taught me.

429
00:30:20,060 --> 00:30:22,460
Then don't disappoint your teacher today.

430
00:30:22,780 --> 00:30:24,380
Yes, teacher.

431
00:30:52,690 --> 00:30:57,200
Why so surprised?

432
00:30:57,230 --> 00:31:01,060
Thought I wouldn't make it out of those woods alive?

433
00:31:03,150 --> 00:31:03,950
You.

434
00:31:04,500 --> 00:31:05,300
That's right,

435
00:31:06,190 --> 00:31:06,990
it's me.

436
00:31:11,750 --> 00:31:13,940
I went to see your brother.

437
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:16,410
And heard the story

438
00:31:16,410 --> 00:31:18,500
your Alpha brother told.

439
00:31:19,980 --> 00:31:21,440
It was quite fascinating.

440
00:31:22,650 --> 00:31:27,030
That's good. Since everyone knows the truth,

441
00:31:27,060 --> 00:31:30,260
no one has to be fooled anymore.

442
00:31:34,470 --> 00:31:35,560
Saengnuea.

443
00:31:36,930 --> 00:31:39,060
Are you really the one behind all this?

444
00:31:39,300 --> 00:31:41,300
This is none of your business, Beta.

445
00:31:41,580 --> 00:31:42,650
Shut up.

446
00:31:44,530 --> 00:31:45,330
That's right.

447
00:31:48,130 --> 00:31:49,400
I did all of this.

448
00:31:51,560 --> 00:31:53,720
I destroyed it all with my own hands.

449
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,810
Letting him run the bar,

450
00:31:57,840 --> 00:31:59,260
that little money

451
00:32:00,100 --> 00:32:01,410
wasn't nearly enough.

452
00:32:02,080 --> 00:32:03,480
So I had Tim

453
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:06,040
bring drugs into the bar to sell.

454
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:07,190
As for you, an impulsive

455
00:32:07,190 --> 00:32:08,600
and rebellious Alpha,

456
00:32:09,230 --> 00:32:11,240
I had Mai get close to you.

457
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:13,730
That woman,

458
00:32:14,700 --> 00:32:17,460
when she heard it could get her ex-husband out of prison,

459
00:32:17,460 --> 00:32:18,900
agreed immediately.

460
00:32:23,960 --> 00:32:24,760
That's right.

461
00:32:26,930 --> 00:32:31,680
The bail for a drug case is so high,

462
00:32:31,700 --> 00:32:36,000
selling people only got us this much.

463
00:32:45,460 --> 00:32:47,310
Then we pinned the blame

464
00:32:47,330 --> 00:32:50,080
on you, a hot-headed Alpha.

465
00:32:53,730 --> 00:32:55,860
But that was a human trafficking case.

466
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:59,260
I didn't expect you to get out so quickly.

467
00:33:01,100 --> 00:33:02,000
But then again,

468
00:33:03,900 --> 00:33:05,300
as long as you have money,

469
00:33:06,930 --> 00:33:08,190
anything is possible.

470
00:33:09,230 --> 00:33:12,160
Even the ex-girlfriend of the person who raised you.

471
00:33:12,230 --> 00:33:13,700
You could actually do it.

472
00:33:13,720 --> 00:33:14,520
That's right.

473
00:33:14,600 --> 00:33:15,900
So why couldn't I?

474
00:33:19,760 --> 00:33:21,300
If I didn't sell that woman,

475
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:24,500
where would I get the money to bail Tim out?

476
00:33:27,300 --> 00:33:29,100
Because he's still useful to me.

477
00:33:30,430 --> 00:33:31,940
He's still my tool

478
00:33:32,510 --> 00:33:35,250
to drag all of you to hell.

479
00:33:39,900 --> 00:33:40,700
All of this

480
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:44,360
is because you hate our family.

481
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:46,840
That's right.

482
00:33:46,860 --> 00:33:49,140
It was the Devathitirat family that caused

483
00:33:49,140 --> 00:33:50,470
my family to go bankrupt

484
00:33:53,150 --> 00:33:55,790
and lose everything.

485
00:33:59,980 --> 00:34:06,700
You have everything. Money, fame, power.

486
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:08,610
You can do whatever you want.

487
00:34:09,820 --> 00:34:13,500
But my family was destroyed and left with nothing.

488
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:16,760
Not even our dignity.

489
00:34:18,500 --> 00:34:21,030
I don't even have the dignity of a human being.

490
00:34:23,139 --> 00:34:26,139
I want to see your whole family completely destroyed,

491
00:34:27,260 --> 00:34:29,060
with not a shred of dignity left.

492
00:34:29,420 --> 00:34:31,420
I want to watch you lose everything.

493
00:34:34,730 --> 00:34:35,900
I want you to suffer

494
00:34:37,110 --> 00:34:38,920
just like I have my whole life.

495
00:34:40,860 --> 00:34:42,400
Even if you've been hurt,

496
00:34:43,860 --> 00:34:46,520
it's no excuse to destroy other people's lives.

497
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:48,960
When my life fell apart,

498
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:51,300
did anyone ask me?

499
00:34:51,929 --> 00:34:53,330
Did anyone ask how I felt?

500
00:34:53,500 --> 00:34:55,100
Did anyone ask if it was fair?

501
00:35:09,930 --> 00:35:11,700
What can a mere Omega

502
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:13,460
even do?

503
00:35:21,700 --> 00:35:22,760
What can I do?

504
00:35:37,360 --> 00:35:39,800
Take care of a stray dog like you, of course.

505
00:35:40,930 --> 00:35:42,530
An ungrateful wretch.

506
00:35:44,300 --> 00:35:45,200
We gave you food

507
00:35:45,860 --> 00:35:46,830
and water,

508
00:35:47,870 --> 00:35:50,530
and you turn around and bite the hand that feeds you.

509
00:35:50,530 --> 00:35:52,660
Where I'm from, we call that an animal.

510
00:35:54,060 --> 00:35:55,100
What did you say?

511
00:35:56,360 --> 00:35:57,470
All this time,

512
00:35:58,760 --> 00:36:01,130
you've tried so hard to act important.

513
00:36:02,860 --> 00:36:04,460
You want people's approval.

514
00:36:06,330 --> 00:36:08,590
You want everyone to think you're great.

515
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:10,730
But in reality,

516
00:36:13,160 --> 00:36:15,100
you're just a watchdog.

517
00:36:21,350 --> 00:36:23,400
Even when you try to beat us,

518
00:36:25,130 --> 00:36:26,640
you only use dirty tricks.

519
00:36:26,660 --> 00:36:27,300
Shut up!

520
00:36:36,660 --> 00:36:37,960
If you have the guts,

521
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:41,200
fight me fair and square.

522
00:36:42,990 --> 00:36:45,050
Don't just hide behind a gun and bark.

523
00:36:50,180 --> 00:36:50,980
Fine.

524
00:37:15,740 --> 00:37:16,920
All of this

525
00:37:18,330 --> 00:37:19,760
is your fault.

526
00:37:20,850 --> 00:37:22,680
You brought the drugs in.

527
00:37:23,850 --> 00:37:25,180
And when you got caught,

528
00:37:26,100 --> 00:37:27,800
you blamed it on someone else.

529
00:37:29,930 --> 00:37:32,660
If you can't figure it out while you're alive,

530
00:37:34,500 --> 00:37:36,030
I'll send you to hell myself

531
00:37:37,330 --> 00:37:38,830
so you can think about it down there.

532
00:37:38,830 --> 00:37:40,730
Whose fault is all this really?

533
00:37:47,940 --> 00:37:48,940
The first shot,

534
00:37:49,770 --> 00:37:50,890
I didn't aim.

535
00:37:53,530 --> 00:37:54,460
But this one,

536
00:37:58,600 --> 00:37:59,700
I did.

537
00:38:34,780 --> 00:38:37,690
Brother, are you hurt badly?

538
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:41,550
I'm fine.

539
00:38:43,730 --> 00:38:44,860
This little scratch

540
00:38:46,060 --> 00:38:47,920
is far from my heart, little hero.

541
00:39:05,930 --> 00:39:06,960
Are you okay?

542
00:39:29,230 --> 00:39:32,570
[In the next episode]

543
00:39:29,330 --> 00:39:32,960
Sila, Ai, and Nakhun got shot!

544
00:39:33,120 --> 00:39:33,920
What?

545
00:39:34,520 --> 00:39:37,550
Mr. Phatsa, you look terrible.

546
00:39:37,600 --> 00:39:38,590
Phatsa, Phatsa.

547
00:39:38,610 --> 00:39:40,050
Nurse!

548
00:39:41,860 --> 00:39:42,910
I came here

549
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:45,260
to apologize for biting Phatsa.

550
00:39:45,500 --> 00:39:47,500
But my son has already formed a bond.

551
00:39:47,660 --> 00:39:49,320
What do you expect me to think?

552
00:39:49,640 --> 00:39:50,870
You're lying.

553
00:39:51,330 --> 00:39:52,640
Impossible.

554
00:39:53,130 --> 00:39:54,430
Why?

555
00:39:55,220 --> 00:39:56,020
Brother.

556
00:39:56,450 --> 00:39:57,250
Saengnuea.

557
00:39:57,280 --> 00:39:59,580
Nakhin, calm down. Don't come closer.

558
00:39:59,890 --> 00:40:00,980
Nakhin.

559
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:19,200
♪ I stay in those beautiful memories. ♪

560
00:40:19,220 --> 00:40:22,560
♪ I thought we were meant to be. ♪

561
00:40:22,880 --> 00:40:24,500
♪ But I also know ♪

562
00:40:24,530 --> 00:40:28,420
♪ that reality isn't like that. ♪

563
00:40:28,540 --> 00:40:32,840
♪ I tried so hard to keep you from leaving. ♪

564
00:40:32,860 --> 00:40:36,290
♪ But our broken love is already shattered. ♪

565
00:40:36,310 --> 00:40:38,750
♪ Because I always believed you would stay. ♪

566
00:40:38,780 --> 00:40:42,750
♪ I'm willing to give up everything for you. ♪

567
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:45,650
♪ We should have had the best future. ♪

568
00:40:45,680 --> 00:40:48,660
♪ But there's no outcome anymore. ♪

569
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:51,670
♪ Only tears are left. ♪

570
